Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||09-01-2001||09:51 PM||||ok... i'm building a motor next spring for my gt... and after going through the whole northstar/lt1 thing, it seems like the 3.4 would be the best way to go. Reality(or my paycheck, however you want to look at it) has made my dreams of either high tech v8 go away.. anyway, the 3.4 is cheap, and supposedly there is very little modification needed for the push-rod version. Anyway, here's my idea, i'm not sure if it would work, thats where you guys come in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>a push-rod 3.4 chevy engine, with a ford thunderbird turbo, and &lt;b&gt;maybe&lt;/b&gt; a 100hp nitrous shot. I'm wondering if the getrag transmission/3.4 block would be able to handle it. My transmission was rebuilt ~30k miles ago, and i would be rebuilding using hp parts, and i'm not going to abuse it(abuse as in redlining, near redlining, burnouts, etc) Anyway, any input would be appreciated. I was also thinking about the sbc but that fricken 250hp 'limit' on the getrag has me worried.<BR>for anyone ready to give the cadillac engine/transmission suggestion, nothing against them, but i really want to stay with a manual transmission.<BR>thanks agian!||||reg||1
